            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0634" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512 Likin/44: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-22T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 22—9:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>786. Legation’s 783, October 17, 8 p.m. Following from Swatow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 19, 1 p.m. My telegram of October 6, noon. Local government
                            likin authorities are now recognizing inward transit certificates. No
                            further action should be taken. Forwarding full report by mail.”<anchor
                                n="76" xml:id="d506-f1"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
